1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,839
The Toothbrush

2
00:00:03,839 --> 00:00:10,140
Once I finish you, my top secret growth potion,

3
00:00:10,419 --> 00:00:13,500
I will create my own giant canine crew!

4
00:00:13,980 --> 00:00:15,500
And then I'll rule the...

5
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:16,039
Whoa!

6
00:00:17,179 --> 00:00:18,900
Wow! This is super!

7
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:20,879
You're better than a TV show!

8
00:00:21,219 --> 00:00:23,740
Oh yeah, it's fun, but it's gonna end badly.

9
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:24,960
Wahahaha!

10
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:26,720
Ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

11
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,440
Tom Thomas, get ready for bed!

12
00:00:30,839 --> 00:00:31,960
I'm going, Dad!

13
00:00:32,719 --> 00:00:34,840
But first, my secret recipe!

14
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:40,760
We start with a bit of carboniterous!

15
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:45,040
And now a little bit of bread and butterous!

16
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:46,439
And finally…

17
00:00:48,439 --> 00:00:50,159
Beardifomerous!

18
00:00:50,159 --> 00:01:00,799
Don't be afraid. Drink, my baby, and you'll grow ten times your size.

19
00:01:01,359 --> 00:01:03,359
What? It doesn't taste good?

20
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,439
Oh, right! I forgot it needed stirring.

21
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,640
This hypersonic mixer will do the trick.

22
00:01:12,759 --> 00:01:15,879
Tom Thomas, you shouldn't use what doesn't belong to you.

23
00:01:16,120 --> 00:01:17,479
That's your father's toothbrush!

24
00:01:21,159 --> 00:01:22,039
Ah!

25
00:01:22,519 --> 00:01:23,679
Hey, cut it out!

26
00:01:24,239 --> 00:01:25,439
You're acting crazy!

27
00:01:30,879 --> 00:01:32,000
Boom!

28
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:34,239
Boom! Boom-boom!

29
00:01:39,679 --> 00:01:40,879
Uh-oh!

30
00:01:41,239 --> 00:01:42,319
You said it!

31
00:01:42,479 --> 00:01:43,599
Uh-oh!

32
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:47,199
You, Tom Thomas, are a big boy, but your brain is smaller than Nolik's.

33
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:48,479
Why, thank you!

34
00:01:49,320 --> 00:01:53,159
Just go put the toothbrush back in its place, um, like you never touched it.

35
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:55,439
Nah, that's not right at all.

36
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,800
Tom Thomas, what's up?

37
00:01:58,159 --> 00:01:59,480
I'm almost done, Dad.

38
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:02,159
Simka, Nolik, please, I really need your help.

39
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:03,120
No panicking!

40
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:06,200
First we need to understand what could have broken inside of there.

41
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:14,080
An electric toothbrush is really simple, as long as you know these three parts.

42
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:15,319
The battery,

43
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:16,360
the motor,

44
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:22,080
and a very clever mechanism that connects the motor with the bristles.

45
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:25,120
The whole secret to the toothbrush is right in there.

46
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:28,560
That mechanism uses the spinning of the motor

47
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:32,160
to make the bristles move very fast back and forth,

48
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:34,320
from left to right, from right to left.

49
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:36,440
And that's how it brushes your teeth.

50
00:02:39,240 --> 00:02:40,800
So what can we do about it?

51
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:42,480
Here's what we do.

52
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:44,360
First we take out the motor,

53
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:46,280
then we take the gears out.

54
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:47,960
And then the mechanism.

55
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:49,760
How much time do we need to do that?

56
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:51,000
One or two hours.

57
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,880
What? No!

58
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:54,600
Just listen here, Tom Thomas.

59
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:56,800
You need to open up the battery compartment.

60
00:02:59,040 --> 00:03:00,520
Wait for me right here.

61
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:06,600
These are your teeth.

62
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:10,080
Well, I mean they're not your teeth, but you get what I'm saying.

63
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:14,000
Nowadays we use a toothbrush to clean our teeth, but it wasn't always that way.

64
00:03:14,639 --> 00:03:19,080
The ancient Egyptians used a chewed stick to scrape their teeth,

65
00:03:19,319 --> 00:03:23,599
while the ancient Greeks rubbed their teeth with a rag.

66
00:03:23,719 --> 00:03:27,240
And the Vikings, well, who knows what they used!

67
00:03:27,319 --> 00:03:30,120
And then, only 200 years ago,

68
00:03:30,199 --> 00:03:34,159
an Englishman named William Addis came up with something better.

69
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:36,560
He drilled holes into a meat bone,

70
00:03:36,639 --> 00:03:39,039
inserted bunches of bristles into them,

71
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:41,719
and there you go – the toothbrush!

72
00:03:42,639 --> 00:03:45,319
And here's what I need to tell you all as a Fixie.

73
00:03:45,439 --> 00:03:47,800
That is, as a master repairman,

74
00:03:47,960 --> 00:03:50,280
you need to make sure to brush your teeth often,

75
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:51,840
especially after eating,

76
00:03:51,919 --> 00:03:54,400
or you'll be getting them repaired often at the dentist!

77
00:03:56,639 --> 00:03:59,199
Well? Is something wrong with the mechanism?

78
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:00,520
No, it's fine.

79
00:04:00,599 --> 00:04:02,199
Is the motor burned out?

80
00:04:02,439 --> 00:04:03,400
No!

81
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:04,800
Then what's wrong with it?

82
00:04:05,639 --> 00:04:07,159
You're not going to believe it.

83
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:09,199
But the battery died!

84
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:10,639
That's all?

85
00:04:10,639 --> 00:04:13,319
I know what to do! I'll put in new ones!

86
00:04:19,159 --> 00:04:21,959
Shhh! Your dad turned the toothbrush on.

87
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:23,959
Looks like everything is fine.

88
00:04:24,279 --> 00:04:25,319
It's working!

89
00:04:26,959 --> 00:04:28,039
Way to go!

90
00:04:28,399 --> 00:04:29,240
Excellent!

91
00:04:29,479 --> 00:04:33,159
Your dad will never find out what kind of slop you mixed up with his brush!

92
00:04:36,319 --> 00:04:37,399
What slop?

93
00:04:37,399 --> 00:04:39,719
Wa-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

94
00:04:40,039 --> 00:04:41,279
How dare you, Nolik!

95
00:04:41,399 --> 00:04:44,399
How dare you refer to my mighty potion like this!

96
00:04:44,560 --> 00:04:47,839
Tom Thomas, somehow soap got all over my toothbrush.

97
00:04:48,079 --> 00:04:49,239
Can you explain that?

98
00:04:51,479 --> 00:04:52,719
Ay-yi-yi!

99
00:04:54,719 --> 00:04:56,679
Well, you got caught!

100
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,479
What do you say now?

